`var` is function-scoped, so the loop has one shared `i`. The `setTimeout` callbacks run after the loop finishes, when `i` is already 3, and each callback reads that same variable.

Fix: use `let`, which creates a fresh binding per iteration:

```js
for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  setTimeout(() => console.log(i), 0);
}
```
